  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of Member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The new Decent Work Country Programme 2023-2027 (scheduled for signature in 2023) includes a specific output that addresses issues raised by the ILO CEACR and CAS on the application of ILO Convention No. 105 on Abolition of Forced Labour -	Provision of technical guidance on the importance of addressing C105 issues over the next DWCP period during drafting meetings with working groups; 
-	Advocacy and training on ILS and the supervisory system; and
-	Provision of technical assistance to address comments of the supervisory bodies on application of Article 1(a) of C105, including through: one-on-one meetings with the government, employers and workers, training on C105 and C29 and P29, development of a technical guidance note, formulation of recommendations to address comments of the supervisory bodies in both law and in practice, development of a legislative review with recommendations and a roadmap for addressing SB comments through legislative reforms.</narrative>
   </description>
